cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use contamsens, please cite it as below."
title: "contamsens: Contamination Sensitivity Analysis for Benchmark Claims"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-07-17
authors:
  - family-names: Joarder
    given-names: Tanvir Anjum
    email: ussash93@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Rajshahi University of Engineering & Technology"
abstract: >-
  Partial identification and sensitivity analysis for machine-learning
  evaluation under unmeasured training-data contamination. Computes, for any
  leaderboard claim, the contamination robustness value Gamma* -- the minimum
  contamination strength that would overturn the claim -- from published
  scores alone, with no reference models, reference benchmarks, or training
  corpus access required.
keywords:
  - benchmark contamination
  - partial identification
  - sensitivity analysis
  - evaluation methodology
license: MIT
